breathing like a singer

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.130
and it looks really good.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:04.963
- Like a human.

00:01:04.963 --> 00:01:06.305
- Yeah. Yeah

00:01:06.305 --> 00:01:07.138
(both laugh)

00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:08.550
Then it's always like
suck it in but I can't.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.610
- Yeah, totally.

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.800
- Wait, but I heard you just
got your driver's license.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.784
- I did.
(audience applauds)

00:01:12.784 --> 00:01:14.510
- That's amazing!

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.730
Were you afraid to get yours?

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.290
I was a little afraid to get mine,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.830
'cause I was afraid of other drivers.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.741
- Right, I was afraid of myself,

00:01:22.741 --> 00:01:23.880
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.400
I mean, I think my mom
was so afraid for me.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.800
Like she was just like,
you are too distracted.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.510
You're just too much Pisces energy

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.740
to be on the highway.
(audience laughs)

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.320
And so I was like, yeah,
you're probably right.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.300
You're probably right.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.950
But then I was like, I
think I spent so much time

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.790
like feeling like I was
like really, really young.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.740
And then I think me
getting my driver's license

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.557
was part of me being like,
you know, I trust myself.

00:01:50.557 --> 00:01:52.250
- I'm a grown woman.
- I'm a grown ass woman.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.560
I can do this.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.910
- Watch this, watch this.
(audience applauds)

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.320
Mine was never me.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.530
I was always afraid of other drivers

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.730
and like big highways
with like mixed masters.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:03.010
I was like, bridges, I
don't think I breathed.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.550
- I'm still scared of highways though.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.060
Like I drove here,

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.460
and every time I drive on the highway,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:10.300
I'm like, you know how like on the maps

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.940
it's like the option without the highways,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.170
and then I'm always like,
damn, it's like twice as long,

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.500
but the whole time I'm on the highway,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.380
my butt is clenched.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.552
I'm like today, is the day I'm gonna die.

00:02:22.552 --> 00:02:23.600
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.433
Today is the day

00:02:24.433 --> 00:02:25.420
- [Kelly] You did it, you made it.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.606
- Yeah.

00:02:26.606 --> 00:02:27.439
- We're proud of you.

00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:28.272
So, wait, did you have
bad dreams about driving?

00:02:28.272 --> 00:02:29.150
I heard that you had some bad dreams.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:29.983
- Yes. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.816
- What were your dreams?

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:31.649
You just wrecked?

00:02:31.649 --> 00:02:33.610
- My dreams were always
that I was in a car,

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.410
the car was going really, really fast,

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.287
but I didn't know what the PRNDL was,

00:02:39.502 --> 00:02:40.335
(audience laughs)

00:02:40.335 --> 00:02:41.480
I didn't know what the
buttons were on the car,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.780
so I didn't know how to work a car-

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.111
- What did you just say?

00:02:44.111 --> 00:02:45.470
(audience laughs)
- The PRNDL?

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.740
The PRNDL, you know, from
"Suite Life of Zack and Cody"?

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.959
(crowd exclaims and cheers)

00:02:49.959 --> 00:02:50.792
- The PRNDL?

00:02:50.792 --> 00:02:52.780
- Where Mr. Moseby is like
teaching London Tipton

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.927
how to drive-
- You know what?

00:02:53.927 --> 00:02:55.162
- And he's like, the PRNDL!

00:02:55.162 --> 00:02:55.995
(audience laughs)

00:02:55.995 --> 00:02:58.916
- We just discovered our age
difference just now. (laughs)

00:02:58.916 --> 00:02:59.749
(audience laughs)

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:00.797
I was like, wait, what
the hell is a PRNDL?

00:03:00.797 --> 00:03:02.627
- What were your shows that you watched?

00:03:02.627 --> 00:03:04.262
- "Saved By The Bell", ma'am.

00:03:04.262 --> 00:03:05.095
(audience applauds)

00:03:05.095 --> 00:03:07.750
Yeah, (chuckles) I was young
for "Saved By The Bell",

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:08.750
but yes, no that was...

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:09.832
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.832 --> 00:03:11.367
- Yeah, mine was "Suite
Life of Zack and Cody",

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.433
"That's So Raven", anyway, so-
(audience cheers)

00:03:13.433 --> 00:03:14.266
- Okay.

00:03:14.266 --> 00:03:15.671
I know "That's So Raven", I know that one.

00:03:15.671 --> 00:03:16.504
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Okay. Okay. Okay.

00:03:16.504 --> 00:03:17.880
- So anyway, so he calls it the PRNDL,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.180
and then, no, she calls
it the PRNDL, right?

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.013
- [Audience] Yeah.

00:03:21.013 --> 00:03:22.670
- And then he's like, "Oh, would you like

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.180
to listen am or fm?"
(audience laughs)

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.013
Like, AM or FM?

00:03:26.013 --> 00:03:26.846
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:26.846 --> 00:03:27.846
- He makes fun of her.

00:03:27.846 --> 00:03:28.679
But anyway,
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:28.679 --> 00:03:30.190
so I had this recurring nightmare

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.090
that I was driving really fast,
I didn't know how to brake,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.720
I didn't know how to do anything,

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:35.553
and so I was like...

00:03:35.553 --> 00:03:36.400
- [Kelly] Loss of control.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.470
- There's only one way to stop this.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:39.303
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:39.303 --> 00:03:40.160
- Learning how to drive.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.030
- You gotta learn how to drive.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:41.863
- Yeah. Totally.

00:03:41.863 --> 00:03:42.696
Loss of control.

00:03:42.696 --> 00:03:43.650
That's probably what that means, right?

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.970
- I always feel like all of my dreams

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.404
mean loss of control-
- Mean something.

00:03:47.404 --> 00:03:48.237
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:48.237 --> 00:03:50.280
What does it mean when you like
lose your teeth in a dream?

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.175
- I think, isn't that
also loss of control?

00:03:53.175 --> 00:03:54.450
Like you feel like you
have no control over-

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.440
- I guess I always feel
out of control. (laughs)

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.334
- I think everything is loss of control.

00:03:58.334 --> 00:03:59.167
- Yeah.
(both laughing)

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.620
- This is my dream book.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.940
The new album is called "Familia",

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.680
so tell us about it and
why you named it that.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.250
- Well, I think that, you know,

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:06.670
at the beginning of this album,

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.860
I was having such a hard
time, like mental health wise.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.140
I just had like what felt-

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.920
- A lot of us the last
two years, especially.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:13.753
- Totally.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:14.960
I think for me it started even (chuckles)

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.040
before the last two years.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.880
- Yeah, well, then the
last two years didn't help.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.570
- Yeah, no.
- Yeah.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:24.190
- It was kind of just like, I
think just crippling anxiety.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:27.610
That was really hard
for me, and I started...

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.990
I feel like because I was in
that place, I isolated a lot

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:33.580
and I felt like I wasn't really...

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.280
I don't know, I felt like...

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.850
I wrote this line in my album thank yous

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:41.010
but I felt like I almost
needed to be kind of healed

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.840
or in a better place
before I let myself be seen

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.310
or let myself hang out with people

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.170
and be vulnerable and be myself,

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.290
and I feel like this album-

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.123
- I relate to that.

00:04:49.123 --> 00:04:49.956
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.110
- And I feel like this album to me

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:54.590
was me being like, really
trusting people, starting with...

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.840
You know, obviously, it's about
like my actual real family

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:58.840
and like the roots of that,

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.450
but also I feel like the
kind of family that I made

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.950
while making this album

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.680
and opening myself up to
friendships and community,

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.730
and even with my
collaborators in the studio

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:14.330
like, being vulnerable about
what I was feeling and-

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.330
- You're very vulnerable.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.800
I heard you allow them to
read your journal and stuff.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.830
You let them read stuff, right?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:20.750
- Well, I don't like...

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.510
I wouldn't be like, you know,
(audience laughs)

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.500
you have access to my diary-

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.190
- Oh, God, 'cause I'm like, "Nope".

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.400
- Absolutely not.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.233
- Yeah.

00:05:28.233 --> 00:05:30.530
- But at the beginning, every day,

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.570
I would like write in a journal,

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:34.980
and then I would just
like read it to Scott,

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.750
and he would be like,
"Oh that's a cool line.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.300
I feel like we could, you know..."

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.430
- Write a song based on
this lyric or whatever".

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.350
So the whole thing for me was really like,

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.600
I need to be real and
vulnerable with the people,

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.860
like while I'm in the studio,

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.273
'cause sometimes I felt like
even being in the studio,

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.270
it felt sometimes performative for me,

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:56.700
like I wanna prove that I'm a good writer,

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.190
I wanna prove that I'm good.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.183
And this time for me was all about,

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.870
Scott, here's like-

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:03.703
- Where I'm at.

00:06:03.703 --> 00:06:06.580
- The worst part of like
where my thoughts go.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:07.940
- Yeah.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:12.000
- And I feel like that
made my favorite music

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.430
that I've made, and also,

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.900
I feel like they really, my collaborators

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.080
became my brothers in the studio,

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.760
and starting to be open with people,

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.090
like with the collaborators
and like in the studio process,

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.710
extended its way into my real life

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:27.410
where suddenly I was like, oh,

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:28.710
I could be like really anxious

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.140
and still hang out with my friend,

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.783
and just tell them about
(chuckles) my anxiety.

00:06:32.783 --> 00:06:33.616
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:33.616 --> 00:06:34.940
- Instead of being like,
let me cancel because-

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:37.020
- Well, 'cause they're not
rolling in perfect either.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.077
- No.

00:06:38.077 --> 00:06:38.910
- They probably got
their own baggage, yeah.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.250
- And I felt like in my mind,

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.290
maybe it's because I was young,

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.960
I felt like everybody just
did have it more together

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:44.793
than I did.

00:06:44.793 --> 00:06:46.410
- Yeah, I think everyone
goes through that.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:47.247
We all feel that. Yeah.

00:06:47.247 --> 00:06:48.560
- And then you grow up
and you're like, (scoffs)

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.050
everybody (beep) up.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.580
- Everyone is screwed.
(all laughing)

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.330
- Yeah.
- Like we're all in therapy.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:54.163
- Yeah.

00:06:54.163 --> 00:06:56.060
- So wait, so you had huge Latin hits

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.740
but then you moved away
from Latin music world,

00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:58.820
now you're kind of back.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.010
You said a couple years
ago you're now back.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.990
So, does it feel good,
because those are your roots

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.823
and it's kind of...

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:06.392
I feel like something that's
super special about you too.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.225
- Thank you.

00:07:07.225 --> 00:07:08.058
- Like 'cause you can do
all these different things

00:07:08.058 --> 00:07:10.260
in different genres, but it is
something I get excited about

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.400
seeing whenever you
perform, I'm like, "Ooh,

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.790
this is gonna be fun."
- Right. Right, right.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:14.640
- Like, and yeah.
(audience member applauds)

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.070
And it's gonna be
beautiful and passionate,

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:18.630
and I feel like that's what
Latin music kind of brings

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.450
to the table a lot of
times, is like passion and-

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.552
- Yes.

00:07:21.552 --> 00:07:22.385
- Vulnerability and all of that.

00:07:22.385 --> 00:07:25.680
So, was it exciting to kind
of make this album like that?

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.870
- Yeah, I mean, I think
like at the beginning,

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:31.120
I was so almost after Havana, for example,

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.747
which Havana came about
in such an organic way.

00:07:34.747 --> 00:07:35.580
- Which is great.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.010
- And then after when
that had a lot of success,

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.970
I felt like when I would go in

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.960
with kind of like American
producers and writers,

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.010
they were just like here's
Havana version five,

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:44.440
and here's Havana version six-

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.890
- Since you've been gone 2.0,

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:46.950
they'd always try and give me that.

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:47.783
- Right.

00:07:47.783 --> 00:07:48.616
- It was super fun.

00:07:48.616 --> 00:07:52.660
- Yeah, and it's like, this
is very obvious, first of all.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.493
- Yeah.

00:07:53.493 --> 00:07:56.660
- And two, I felt like it
just felt not authentic,

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.370
it felt like they were kind of putting me-

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.203
- And you're chasing it.

00:07:59.203 --> 00:08:02.370
- In this box, and chasing
it and putting me in this box

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.660
because it was successful,

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:04.930
and so I was like, you know,

00:08:04.930 --> 00:08:06.900
I think subconsciously I was
like, I don't wanna do that.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.270
And then I think this album came around

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.830
and in working with Ricky
Reed and Scott Harris,

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:17.750
Ricky introduced me to
like this man named Cheche

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.060
and this writer named Edgar Barerra,

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:23.358
and they're like actually like Latin.

00:08:23.358 --> 00:08:24.191
- Yeah.

00:08:24.191 --> 00:08:25.500
- One is from Argentina
and one is from Mexico.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:26.890
And so actually-

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.330
(audience cheers and applauds)
Yeah.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.100
And so actually being in those sessions

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.580
and being able to be like, okay,

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.030
what kind of songs should we write today?

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:35.620
And then me pulling up a playlist

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:38.180
of like Alejandro
Fernandez, Alejandro Sanz,

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.486
Celia Cruz and like-
(audience applauds)

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:41.350
- It's inspiring!

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.170
- Yeah, and for other
people to be like, oh yeah!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.400
And did you ever hear that one?

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.440
Like, it just made it and
be able to speak Spanish

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.490
in the studio, and-

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:50.500
- It felt authentic.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.410
- It felt authentic,

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.690
it didn't feel like somebody

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:56.380
was just kind of like money grab vibe-

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:57.320
- [Kelly] This was a hit, so well, yeah.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:58.730
- Yeah, totally.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:01.080
So long, I was like,
this doesn't feel right.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.560
And now, I think it
organically went to a place

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.000
where I was like, oh,
this feels right for me,

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:10.370
this feels like I'm getting to speak

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.160
my first language in the studio.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:16.530
I'm getting to be with my people,

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.588
I'm getting to like you know-

00:09:18.588 --> 00:09:19.421
(audience applauds)
- Feels nice.

00:09:19.421 --> 00:09:21.030
- Explore that in a genuine way.

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:25.200
So that made me really
excited about this album too.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.890
- I think you're so transparent
in the best of ways.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:27.840
So I think that that's good.
- Thanks.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:28.830
- You have to like stick true

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:29.840
to like where you are in the moment,

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.620
but thank you for coming to our show.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.071
(audience applauds)

00:09:33.071 --> 00:09:33.991
I'm such a fan.

00:09:33.991 --> 00:09:38.337
- Camila Cabello, y'all,
give it up! (clapping)

